# .gitignore — DFIR Lab Repository

# ===========================================================================
# SECURITY-CRITICAL: Never commit actual forensic evidence to Git
# These files can contain sensitive system information from the VM
# Store them on an encrypted external drive, NOT in the repo
# ===========================================================================

# Memory dumps
*.raw
*.mem
*.elf
*.vmem
*.dmp
*.dump

# Disk images
*.E01
*.img
*.vmdk
*.vdi
*.iso

# Password files or key material (should never exist in this repo)
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx

# ===========================================================================
# Development artifacts
# ===========================================================================

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Editor files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Pandoc / LaTeX build artifacts
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk

# ===========================================================================
# Internal Authoring, Prompt Briefs & Development Scaffolding
# (Files used internally during project build; excluded from public portfolio)
# ===========================================================================
08-ransomware-simulation-forensics.md
PHASE_0_CHECKLIST.md
simulation/SCRIPT_REVIEW_v1.0.md
simulation/CHANGELOG.md

# ===========================================================================
# What IS tracked in Git (Public Portfolio Deliverables)
# ===========================================================================
# - README.md, SAFETY.md, .gitignore
# - docs/INCIDENT_RESPONSE_REPORT.md (primary executive consulting deliverable)
# - screenshots/*.png (all 8 forensic proof and verification screenshots)
# - simulation/custom_behavior_sim.py (ransomware behavior simulation tool)
# - simulation/test_crash_recovery.py (15-test unit suite for atomic recovery)
# - simulation/atomic_red_team_tests.md (MITRE ATT&CK test procedure plan)
# - forensics/acquisition/*.md & *.sha256 (forensic SOPs and cryptographic hashes)
# - forensics/volatility_analysis/ANALYSIS_NOTES.md & *.txt (memory forensics logs)
# - forensics/autopsy_analysis/ANALYSIS_NOTES.md, deleted_files_report.md & *.csv (disk forensics)

